# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# npm config for @lankacom/auth (public npm registry)
#
# For local publishing you usually don't need an .npmrc at all — just run
# `npm login`. The @lankacom scope resolves to the public registry by default.
#
# This example is only for CI / automated publishing with an npm automation
# token. Copy to `.npmrc` and inject NPM_TOKEN via your CI secret store.
# `.npmrc` is gitignored so the token is never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auth for the public npm registry (used by `npm publish` in CI).
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
